  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1144 AM CDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nThe theme of generally quiet weather will continue through the rest \nof the week as the jet stream and upper level storm track remain \ndisplaced well to our north. Most models agree that a weak blocking \npattern will establish over the south-central and SW CONUS Tue-Thu \nwith weak flow aloft prevailing overhead. Surface flow will return \nto a predominantly southerly direction during this period, and above \naverage temperatures are expected each day during the midweek period \nwith highs mainly in the middle 80s. By late week, the pattern is \nprogged to evolve such that a broad mid/upper level low will \nestablish somewhere in the vicinity of the Big Bend region. This \ncould bring a return of light rain chances mainly over southern \nzones by Friday, but ensemble consensus favors dry conditions over \nmost of our area as the best moisture remains well to our south and \nforcing remains subtle given only weak flow aloft locally. Overall, \nexpect a pleasant (but perhaps a bit warm) week across the region.",
